The population distribution is highly uneven. The [[Sant Bart (comarca)|Sant Bart]] comarca, containing the provincial capital, accounts for approximately 40 per cent of the provincial population with a density of 611/km². The [[Costabella (comarca)|Costabella]] comarca, containing the province's second-largest city, accounts for a further 21 per cent with a density of 637/km². The remaining 19 comarcas share approximately 39 per cent of the population, with densities ranging from 5/km² in the remote highland comarca of [[Altbirú (comarca)|Altbirú]] to 283/km² in the semi-urban comarca of [[Altaneu (comarca)|Altaneu]].

== Government ==

{{see also|Politics of Balboa|Administrative divisions of Balboa}}

Jala Province operates within the framework of Balboa's unitary presidential system, with a directly elected governor serving as chief executive and a 57-seat provincial assembly ({{lang|ca|Assemblea Provincial de Jala}}) elected by single transferable vote every four years. The governor is elected by direct popular vote using a two-round system, concurrent with the assembly elections. The provincial government has authority over education, health, provincial transport, and land use planning, within the powers devolved by the national constitution.

[[File:Assemblea Provincial de Jala.png|thumb|right|300px|The Jala Provincial Assembly building in Sant Bart.]]
<!-- IMAGE PROMPT: Provincial parliament building in a tropical highland city, mid-century modern civic architecture, concrete and stone facade, assembly chamber visible through large windows, tropical gardens in foreground, flag poles, photorealistic, overcast highland light -->

=== Governor ===

The current governor is '''Gaspar Mas i Bonet''' of the [[Balboan People's Party]] (BPP), elected in the [[2022 Jala provincial election|2022 provincial election]] and serving a four-year term. Mas, a member of the BPP's Centrist faction, previously served as comissari of the [[Sant Bart (comarca)|Sant Bart comarca]] from 2014 to 2022. His administration has focused on infrastructure investment — particularly the expansion of the [[Badia Curta]] industrial zone and the long-delayed high-speed rail connection to [[Sant Cristòfor]] — and on managing the political tensions between the industrial east and the rural highland comarcas.

Mas defeated the [[Democratic Alliance (Balboa)|Democratic Alliance]] candidate, '''Pere Vidal i Soler''' of the [[Liberal Party of Balboa]], in the second round of the 2022 election, with approximately 54 per cent of the vote. The election was closer than previous provincial contests, reflecting the BPP's declining national dominance.

=== Provincial assembly ===

The Jala Provincial Assembly consists of 57 members elected by STV from multi-member constituencies corresponding to the province's comarcas. The current assembly was elected in 2022 and reflects the fragmentation of Balboan national politics:

